---
title: Yakitori Chicken
servings: 4
course: Main
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Japanese
---

= Yakitori Sauce =

Mix the @sake{4%tbsp}, @soy sauce{5%tbsp}, @mirin (rice wine){1%tbsp}, and @caster sugar{1%tbsp} in a #small saucepan{}. Bring to the boil, then reduce the heat and simmer for ~{10%minutes} until the sauce has thickened.

= Chicken =

Grill the @chicken thighs{8}(boned, cut into 1” cubes) pieces until the juices drip. Dip into the sauce and grill on each side for ~{30%seconds}. Repeat the dipping process twice more.

Set the chicken aside and keep warm. Gently grill the @spring onions{8}(cut into 1” sticks) until soft and slightly brown. (Do no dip the spring onions in the sauce.)

Assemble chicken and spring onions onto skewers. Serve with @lemon{}(cut into wedges).